<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhu Nuwas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dhu Nuwas was a Jewish king of Himyar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a> in the early sixth century, remembered for his persecution of Christians at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najran">Najran</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>, at the request of the Byzantine emperor, sent a naval expedition across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> that defeated him and installed a Christian ruler, extending Aksumite control over South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>.</p></div>
